                                "sense_id": "c1d98a79-d637-3192-a0f4-ac689050ea79",
                                "text": "They themselves live now in the reverence, admiration, and love they feel for the delicate, the private, the domestic nature of woman. They foresee the shrine where they worship profaned; they feel the bosoms where they are warmed growing hard and cold. They see the Homes where alone their public cares are soothed and made tolerable, converted into disprivacied parts of the great Hotel of life."
                            },
